title: 'State: voice-approval reviews (26 Aegis, 27 Arky) and librarian panel (28) landed; founder rulings pending'
summary: |-
  Research 26 (Aegis), 27 (Arky) and 28 (librarian panel) are saved. Aegis and Arky agree on the following:
  - a fresh-presence "voice arm" that binds the approvals-key unlock to one voice connection;
  - the broker signs voice decisions in a separate domain, gnomon:approve-voice:v1, with no new verb;
  - the toggles are root-signed, keyed by repo, never in project.yaml, and turning them off needs no presence;
  - every voice decision has a hold with undo;
  - TTS phrase masking and half-duplex prevent agent self-approval;
  - install, use-api-token, always and voice settings stay hand-only;
  - screen lock drops the arm.

  They diverge on five points, which need the founder:
  - (a) Targeting: Aegis wants secret per-card handle words, shown only on screen or spoken in headphones, which the kernel can verify. Arky wants spoken ordinals and labels against a read-back deck, which works eyes-free but relies on checks the voice client asserts.
  - (b) Gate arm: Aegis wants 5 min, at most 3 decisions, headphones and a 2-word challenge. Arky wants up to 60 min with readback plus confirm, conversation mode allowed.
  - (c) Reversible arm: Aegis wants a 60 min hard cap and 30 decisions. Arky wants 240 min.
  - (d) KNOT resolve and verdicts by voice: Aegis wants a separate sub-opt-in, default off. Arky includes them in toggle 2.
  - (e) Toggle storage: Aegis wants config.yaml; Arky wants grant rows. Recommendation: Arky's grant rows.

  The librarian panel (28) recommends no new agent: activate the existing archivist "Index", widen Loid's memory review to research, specs, lore and decisions, add Rune's dead-reference test, and put branches and stashes on Cid's board. That also awaits the founder. Next: rulings, then spec v3.4, then the aesthetic boards.
